1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,403
Deaf and hard-of-hearing people miss the
sounds that matter at home:

2
00:00:05,453 --> 00:00:07,677
the door, the alarm, the baby.

3
00:00:07,727 --> 00:00:11,693
Sound Sense is a small box for the table
by the door.

4
00:00:11,743 --> 00:00:15,027
It listens, alerts on its screen and
lights,

5
00:00:15,077 --> 00:00:19,650
and runs entirely on this Alif E8 board.
Nothing is recorded.

6
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,148
Every start runs a self-test:

7
00:00:22,198 --> 00:00:26,323
both microphones, the neural processor
against a stored reference,

8
00:00:26,373 --> 00:00:29,740
the saved sounds, the vibration sensor and
the lights.

9
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:32,650
It's ready one and a half seconds after
reset.

10
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,909
The home screen shows what it hears:

11
00:00:35,959 --> 00:00:41,967
a spectrogram, the room level against its
noise floor, and the three best matches.

12
00:00:42,017 --> 00:00:45,218
In a quiet room the NPU rests to save
power.

13
00:00:45,268 --> 00:00:49,650
When I talk, the encoder wakes up and the
matches come back.

14
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,219
Seven sounds are built in:

15
00:00:52,269 --> 00:00:57,011
knock, dog, baby, alarm, glass, siren and
running water. Here's an alarm:

16
00:00:57,061 --> 00:01:01,869
a full-screen card with an icon, a word
and the time, in colours that work

17
00:01:01,919 --> 00:01:06,267
with colour blindness, and the lights
flash a pattern of their own.

18
00:01:06,317 --> 00:01:11,650
Urgent sounds, like breaking glass, strobe
once a second and stay until you press.

19
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:16,312
Here's what a microphone alone can't do.

20
00:01:16,362 --> 00:01:21,998
I knock on the table, twenty centimetres
from the board.

21
00:01:22,048 --> 00:01:27,380
The accelerometer, read eight hundred
times a second,

22
00:01:27,430 --> 00:01:33,372
feels it, and the microphones hear it:
felt here and heard.

23
00:01:33,422 --> 00:01:40,683
Now the same knock from the laptop, held
in the air, like a knock on TV.

24
00:01:40,733 --> 00:01:48,604
The microphones hear it, but nothing
touched the table, so it's only a banner:

25
00:01:48,654 --> 00:01:51,650
heard only.

26
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:59,016
Every home sounds different, so you teach
it your own.

27
00:01:59,066 --> 00:02:05,657
Press up, pick a name, here Keys, and
press to start.

28
00:02:05,707 --> 00:02:09,416
I jingle my keys eight times.

29
00:02:09,466 --> 00:02:13,175
Each example is checked:

30
00:02:13,225 --> 00:02:21,570
too quiet, clipped, a loud room, or unlike
the others gets flagged,

31
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:28,587
and a good one turns green with its level
over the room.

32
00:02:28,637 --> 00:02:32,472
One more jingle tests it. Save.

33
00:02:32,522 --> 00:02:36,231
No laptop and no retraining:

34
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:44,125
the board builds a profile from the NPU's
embeddings, and saves

35
00:02:44,175 --> 00:02:50,891
it to flash in the background without
missing a sound.

36
00:02:50,941 --> 00:02:54,650
And now it knows my keys.

37
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,209
Now I reset the board.

38
00:02:58,259 --> 00:03:05,606
The self-test restores the taught sounds
from flash in under a millisecond.

39
00:03:05,656 --> 00:03:09,650
Jingle again, and it still knows my keys.

40
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:13,460
Left shows today's timeline:

41
00:03:13,510 --> 00:03:19,452
every sound, with repeats merged and felt
knocks marked.

42
00:03:19,502 --> 00:03:23,197
If it got one wrong, left marks it.

43
00:03:23,247 --> 00:03:31,650
That sound becomes a counter-example, so
it won't set off the same alert again.

44
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:35,565
Right shows the numbers, live from the
board.

45
00:03:35,615 --> 00:03:40,794
The encoder is our own PyTorch model,
quantized to int8 and run through

46
00:03:40,844 --> 00:03:44,992
ExecuTorch, with all fourteen operators on
the Ethos-U85:

47
00:03:45,042 --> 00:03:47,202
about one millisecond per run.

48
00:03:47,252 --> 00:03:50,517
In a quiet room the CPU is awake twelve
point

49
00:03:50,567 --> 00:03:53,831
six percent of the time, down from a
hundred.

50
00:03:53,881 --> 00:03:59,650
Sound Sense learns your home, feels your
door, and keeps your sounds to itself.

